## Conversation
The user asked for a minimal DFlash2 implementation based on z-lab/dflash and the TorchSpec DFlash and DSpark pull requests, with tests and a draft pull request. After the first implementation commit, read-only critics found sparse selector supervision, weak tests, incorrect online serving export, missing target-layer derivation, and configuration boundary gaps.

## Actions
Replaced top-K-hit-only selector supervision with teacher-forced sampled cross-entropy over the gold successor and the strongest top-K negatives. Added prefix masking and a cross-rank denominator. Reused model-owned serving config and state-dict hooks in both online saving and offline conversion. Derived omitted target layer IDs, validated convolution geometry and capture layers, corrected the shared mask helper and zero-loss hook, and expanded focused tests from 11 to 18. Ran Ruff, formatting, the focused suite, a 107-test DFlash/DFlash2/DSpark regression suite with a local Mooncake import stub, and an online serving-save smoke.

## Errors & Mistakes
The first implementation trained the selector only when the gold token was already in the unary top K. At production vocabulary and top-K sizes this would usually produce no selector gradient at initialization. The first tests also did not exercise the finish half of dynamic convolution or independently verify selector alignment. The first manual serving helper smoke tried to instantiate the abstract Trainer class and failed with TypeError: Can not instantiate abstract class Trainer without an implementation for abstract methods; the smoke was rerun through DFlash2Trainer and passed.

## Dead Ends
Masking selector rows whose gold token missed top K was abandoned because it starved the selector before the unary model had useful recall. Duplicating the offline converter inside DFlash2Trainer was rejected in favor of model-owned serialization hooks shared by both save paths. A full-vocabulary selector loss was not used because its memory and compute cost would be impractical.

## Hints for Future Agents
The selector objective is a TorchSpec-defined sampled objective because upstream revision 07ebd93 publishes inference code only. Keep the pull request explicit about that boundary. DFlash2Config subclasses DFlashConfig, so dispatch must remain before DFlash. The official top-level num_target_layers is target depth, while TorchSpec internally uses num_target_layers for the number of captured layers. Mooncake has no macOS ARM wheel, so local related-suite runs need an import-only stub; do not describe that as a production Mooncake test.

## Codebase Discoveries
The online scratch-checkpoint and weight-sync path calls Trainer.save_draft_model_for_serving directly and does not invoke tools/convert_to_hf.py. Serving therefore needs qwen3 model_type and fc, hidden_norm, and norm keys at model-save time. Composable REPLICATE fails on unused trainable selector parameters, so the selector loss weight is required to be positive. The official inference selector score uses the verified predecessor token, projected draft hidden state, unary candidate logit, and successor codebook.

## Open Questions
Upstream does not disclose the selector training loss, initialization recipe, optimizer schedule, or convergence results. No CUDA, multi-rank, SGLang, or convergence run was available in this macOS worktree. The sampled selector objective needs empirical validation before claiming training parity with released DFlash2 checkpoints.
